ladimir Nevzorov"] " (URS) had begun his sporting career as a wrestler, like many " [:em {} "judoka"] ", but by 1976 was a heavy favorite to win gold in Montréal in judo. He had won the 1975 World and European Championships. Japan’s representative in the class was " [:a {:href "/athletes/33961"} "Koji Kuramoto"] ", bronze medalist at the 1975 Worlds. There were no surprises as these two made it to the final, with Nevzorov winning all his early bouts by " [:em {} "ippon"] ". The final was not close, although Kuramoto survived for the duration. But Nevzorov was the top " [:em {} "judoka"] " in Montréal and thoroughly dominated his Japanese foe. This ended Nevzorov’s short, but meteoric, career. He never again competed internationally."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34144"} "Vladimir Nevzorov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/33961"} "Koji Kuramoto"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34503"} "Patrick Vial"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34442"} "Marian Tał